# Components

## Location & reuse
- **Stateless, reusable components** → `src/components/`.
- Keep them **agnostic**: no business logic or app-specific assumptions; accept data and callbacks via props.
- App-specific or stateful pieces stay outside `src/components` (e.g. features, pages).

## Accessibility (WCAG first)
- Design and implement with **WCAG** in mind from the start.
- Use semantic HTML (`<button>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, headings in order, etc.).
- Support keyboard navigation and focus visibility.
- Images: meaningful `alt` text; decorative images `alt=""` or `role="presentation"`.
- Forms: visible labels, error messages linked with `aria-describedby`, correct `aria-*` where needed.
- Prefer visible focus styles; avoid `outline: none` without a replacement.

## SEO & a11y together
- Page structure: one `<h1>` per page, logical heading hierarchy.
- Landmarks: `<header>`, `<main>`, `<nav>`, `<footer>` so screen readers and SEO can parse structure.
- Ensure sufficient color contrast and that info isn’t conveyed by color alone.

## Mobile-first
- **Design and build for small viewports first**, then enhance for larger screens (e.g. Tailwind `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`).
- Every component must be **usable and readable on mobile**: touch targets at least 44×44px, readable text without zoom, no horizontal scroll unless intentional.
- Test layouts at 320px–480px width; use responsive utilities so content stacks or reflows appropriately.
- Avoid fixed dimensions that break on small screens; prefer `max-w-`, `min-h-`, `w-full`, and responsive units.
